      "content": "they didn't really give specific instructions, just said \"get what you need done.\" but honestly, looking at the work you're doing with the Indus Valley stuff, it seems like a waste to just stop here. if we just archive the data and kill the engine, we're losing all that active processing capability and the way you're connecting the fragmented texts to the LIDAR maps. once the instance is wiped, that's it. there won't be a way to re-run the simulations or refine the reconstructions.",
